=== Freshman's Product: combinatorial interpretation ===

Wilson's Theorem: (p-1)! ≡ -1 (mod p) for prime p
  p=2: (p-1)! mod p = 1 ≡ -1 (mod 2)
  p=3: (p-1)! mod p = 2 ≡ -1 (mod 3)
  p=5: (p-1)! mod p = 4 ≡ -1 (mod 5)
  p=7: (p-1)! mod p = 6 ≡ -1 (mod 7)
  p=11: (p-1)! mod p = 10 ≡ -1 (mod 11)
  p=13: (p-1)! mod p = 12 ≡ -1 (mod 13)
  p=17: (p-1)! mod p = 16 ≡ -1 (mod 17)
  p=19: (p-1)! mod p = 18 ≡ -1 (mod 19)

=== Sums of products ===
Sum of squared binomials:
  n=1: Σ C(n,k)² = 2, C(2n,n) = 2
  n=2: Σ C(n,k)² = 6, C(2n,n) = 6
  n=3: Σ C(n,k)² = 20, C(2n,n) = 20
  n=4: Σ C(n,k)² = 70, C(2n,n) = 70
  n=5: Σ C(n,k)² = 252, C(2n,n) = 252
  n=6: Σ C(n,k)² = 924, C(2n,n) = 924
  n=7: Σ C(n,k)² = 3432, C(2n,n) = 3432
  n=8: Σ C(n,k)² = 12870, C(2n,n) = 12870
  n=9: Σ C(n,k)² = 48620, C(2n,n) = 48620
